 AIDS</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12590791</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050092-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bharucha</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Sastry</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrotri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Joshi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Feasibility of voluntary counselling and testing services for HIV among pregnant women presenting in labour in Pune, India</article-title><source>Int J STD AIDS</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>553</fpage><lpage>555</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16105190</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050092-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jamieson</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Sullivan</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Maupin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Webber</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The challenges of informed consent for rapid HIV testing in labor</article-title><source>J Womens Health (Larchmt)</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>889</fpage><lpage>895</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14670168</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050092-b013"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>&#x0005b;No authors listed&#x0005d;</collab><year>2006</year><source>Orasure Technologies OraQuick ADVANCE Rapid HIV1/2 Antibody Test (package insert)</source><publisher-loc>Orasure Technologies, Bethelem, Pennsylvania</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Orasure Technologies</publisher-name></citation